findings.proposed_change:
Extract the following deterministic statement, retaining actualFactorStops_regular as a convenience theorem:

lemma actualFactorStops_monotone {Ω ι : Type*}
    {U : Ω → ℝ≥0 → ℝ} {γ : Ω → ℝ≥0 → ℂ}
    {G F : Ω → ℝ≥0 → ℂ → ℂ}
    (hU : ∀ ω, Continuous (U ω))
    (hw : ∀ ω, IsCapacityTwoWitness (U ω) (γ ω) (G ω) (F ω))
    (z : ι → ℂ) (u₀ u₂ : ι → ℝ)
    (h₀ : ∀ i, 0 ≤ u₀ i) (hu : ∀ i, u₀ i ≤ u₂ i) (H : ℝ≥0) :
    ∀ ω i, Monotone (fun k => actualFactorStops γ G z u₀ u₂ H (i,k) ω)

Reuse lines 72–77, replacing continuous_const.mul (hBc ω') with hU ω'. The existing factorRadiusLevel_nonneg and factorRadiusLevel_monotone discharge the level assumptions of radiusLevelTime_mono; cutoffStop_mono then preserves the ordering. Equal endpoint levels remain valid because monotonicity is non-strict. Unreached levels are handled by the existing extended-time lemma and cutoff, and empty Ω or ι makes the conclusion vacuous.

